  "note": "Re-recorded by Sprint-5 wave 2 (2026-09-10). The move was earned by ANA-10's in-Python config resolution (11.45): module-level dict literals, dataclass field defaults, argparse `default=` and the attribute/subscript chains rooted at them now resolve to literals, so `CFG[\"workers\"]` and `cfg.data.workers` read like `4` does. Measured A/B on this tree with `ir.bindings._resolve_config` monkeypatched to a no-op: overall recall 0.7179 -> 0.7308, visible 0.6410 -> 0.6538, high+medium 0.6316 -> 0.6491, unseen 0.5319 -> 0.5532, graph fidelity 126 -> 127 of 139 (the `getattr` selection node makes hydra_research's optimizer_for(...) resolve to an optimizer). The single new finding is a planted defect, MLV201 at hydra_research/src/train.py:35. Precision stays 1.0 in both dataflow modes and forbidden findings stay 0; a config read can never mint a `certain` finding, because every read costs one CONFIG_EVIDENCE_WEIGHT = 0.8 factor and 0.98 x 0.8 = 0.784. H5 (11.42) is finding-neutral by construction and moved nothing here: it adds one optional `Issue.fix` field to five existing findings and touches no rule gate, evidence or confidence. Recall may only ratchet up; a forbidden finding is never tolerated. Regenerate with `python tools/accuracy.py --update-baseline` and say in the commit body which change earned the new number.",
